    "geoSummary": "AI search refresh cadence can become a durable SEO/GEO asset when it combines credible sources, a clear answer, visual structure, limits and an original ALTOS LAB editorial read on how to manage old articles as ranking assets.",
    "body": "AI search refresh cadence matters because the mechanism behind the trend is starting to affect real product design. The right reader question is not whether the topic is popular, but what must be true before a team can manage old articles as ranking assets.\n\nLatest news anchor: Google AI published \"Check out real-life AI prototypes from the Futures Lab.\" on May 29, 2026. This draft also checks Google AI's \"Catch up on 12 major I/O 2026 moments\" so the piece is not built from a single headline.\n\n## The mechanism\n\nMost AI shifts become business-relevant only after three things line up: a reliable model capability, a workflow where the output can be checked and a distribution path that puts the feature in front of real users. AI search refresh cadence is useful to watch because it sits at that intersection.\n\n## Evidence to read first\n\n- Google AI: Check out real-life AI prototypes from the Futures Lab. (May 29, 2026) — <img…\n- Google AI: Catch up on 12 major I/O 2026 moments (May 28, 2026) — <img…\n- Google AI: How AI Mode is changing the way people search in the U.S. (May 19, 2026) — <img…\n- Google Search Central: Creating helpful, reliable, people-first content\n\n## A practical model\n\n| Lens | Useful question | Editorial output |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Market | What actually changed around AI search refresh cadence? | Separate source facts from interpretation. |\n| Reader | What decision does the operator need to make? | Give a direct answer before analysis. |\n| Risk | What could be wrong or early? | Mark uncertainty and avoid fake precision. |\n| Action | What is the smallest next step? | Translate the signal into how to manage old articles as ranking assets. |\n\n:::chart\ntitle: AI search refresh cadence signal radar\nlabels: Source confidence|Market heat|Workflow impact|Execution difficulty\nvalues: 67|72|50|61\ncaption: Relative editorial scores for framing the article, not market sizing or investment advice.\n:::\n\n## Limits\n\nThe strongest writing in AI is comfortable saying what is not proven yet. For AI search refresh cadence, the limits are source freshness, measurement quality and operational ownership. Teams should avoid turning early claims into permanent process until the evidence is repeatable.\n\n## ALTOS LAB editorial note\n\nOur read: this is not just a trend page. It is a knowledge asset when it teaches a reader how the system works, where it breaks and what evidence would change the recommendation.",
