    "body": "Model routing strategy is easy to describe and harder to use. The uncomfortable point: many teams will lose time by reacting to the headline before they know which decision the trend actually changes.\n\nLatest news anchor: OpenAI published \"Strengthening societal resilience with Rosalind Biodefense\" on May 29, 2026. This draft also checks Google AI's \"Check out real-life AI prototypes from the Futures Lab.\" so the piece is not built from a single headline.\n\n## The common misread\n\nAI markets reward speed, so every update can feel urgent. But urgency is not the same as priority. Model routing strategy deserves attention only if it changes a customer expectation, a cost line, a product workflow or a measurable risk.\n\n## What the sources actually support\n\n- OpenAI: Strengthening societal resilience with Rosalind Biodefense (May 29, 2026) — OpenAI launches Rosalind Biodefense, expanding trusted access to GPT-Rosalind for vetted developers and U.S…\n- Google AI: Check out real-life AI prototypes from the Futures Lab. (May 29, 2026) — <img…\n- Google AI: Catch up on 12 major I/O 2026 moments (May 28, 2026) — <img…\n- OpenAI: OpenAI News\n\n## A sharper way to frame it\n\n| Lens | Useful question | Editorial output |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Market | What actually changed around Model routing strategy? | Separate source facts from interpretation. |\n| Reader | What decision does the operator need to make? | Give a direct answer before analysis. |\n| Risk | What could be wrong or early? | Mark uncertainty and avoid fake precision. |\n| Action | What is the smallest next step? | Translate the signal into how to allocate model cost by task difficulty and risk. |\n\n## Signal chart\n\n:::chart\ntitle: Model routing strategy signal radar\nlabels: Source confidence|Market heat|Workflow impact|Execution difficulty\nvalues: 81|86|64|75\ncaption: Relative editorial scores for framing the article, not market sizing or investment advice.\n:::\n\n## The better question\n\nInstead of asking whether to chase Model routing strategy, ask what evidence would make the team change behavior this month. If the answer is vague, keep watching. If the answer is concrete, write the small experiment.\n\n## ALTOS LAB point of view\n\nALTOS LAB should sound opinionated without pretending to know more than the sources allow. A strong column names the tradeoff, shows the evidence and leaves the reader with a cleaner judgment.",
